GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "CA0B4E4026C30C25"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{EC5CB743DBDBC5A4}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Summary"
     m_sContent "British forces must sweep and secure a series of farmyards along an MSR that have been used by the Irish Republican Army to conduct sporadic attacks against passing convoys and occasional civilian traffic."\
     ""\
     "Can British forces clear the area, deny the IRA use of these positions, and restore freedom of movement along the MSR?"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Summary Notes</h2>"\
     "• UK 3minute setup timer."
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{82C3CD6A62572A2B}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 21/07/1991, 0600hrs, Northern Ireland."\
     "Weather: Clear, light winds, visibility 1km+, with forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
     "Operation Banner remains ongoing as British forces continue to support the Royal Ulster Constabulary in maintaining security and disrupting paramilitary activity across Northern Ireland."\
     ""\
     "Over recent months, IRA personnel have repeatedly used three isolated farmyards overlooking the Main Supply Route (MSR) between Lovetin and Kamoryn to conduct ambushes against British Army patrols, Royal Ulster Constabulary units, and, on occasion, civilian traffic. The locations are not permanently occupied, with personnel moving in and out using irregular patterns to avoid detection."\
     ""\
     "Following weeks of surveillance and intelligence gathering, C Company has been tasked with conducting a coordinated search operation to clear the suspected locations, deny the IRA use of the farmyards, and restore freedom of movement along the route."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{4D7910ACC998B3B6}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 21/07/1991, 0600hrs, Northern Ireland."\
     "Weather: Clear, light winds, visibility 1km+, with forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
     "Operation Banner remains ongoing as British forces continue to support the Royal Ulster Constabulary in maintaining security and disrupting paramilitary activity across Northern Ireland."\
     ""\
     "Over recent months, IRA personnel have repeatedly used three isolated farmyards overlooking the Main Supply Route (MSR) between Lovetin and Kamoryn to conduct ambushes against British Army patrols, Royal Ulster Constabulary units, and, on occasion, civilian traffic. The locations are not permanently occupied, with personnel moving in and out using irregular patterns to avoid detection."\
     ""\
     "Following weeks of surveillance and intelligence gathering, C Company has been tasked with conducting a coordinated search operation to clear the suspected locations, deny the IRA use of the farmyards, and restore freedom of movement along the route."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRA"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{BD8A5341336A7C7E}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "Enemy forces consist of the Irish Republican Army (IRA), operating throughout the marked area of operations. Intelligence estimates enemy strength up to 35 personnel. This assessment is based on close target reconnaissance of ambush sites, reports from British and Garda convoys, and information provided by the local population."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2> "\
     "• Reports from convoys indicate the IRA has employed heavy machine guns from elevated positions providing effective fields of fire over the MSR."\
     "• Regular use of explosive charges and booby traps."\
     "• Knowledge of the local terrain and established ambush positions particularly overlooking the MSR and its key approaches."\
     "• Expect a lightly equipped but highly mobile force capable of conducting well-coordinated hit-and-run engagements before breaking contact."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9A17A7A0445CD2F0}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "Enemy forces consist of British Army elements operating throughout the marked area of operations. Their strength is estimated at approximately 40 personnel, consisting primarily of light infantry supported by a small number of mobile elements."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• All British personnel are equipped with weapon optics."\
     "• The British hold an overall advantage in firepower, numbers, and mobility."\
     "• They are operating 4x WMIKs, each equipped with a roof-mounted .50 cal heavy machine gun and a forward-mounted GPMG, providing significant mobile firepower."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRA"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C714BB76D5010A69}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "We are the British Army."\
     "Consisting of light infantry from 2 Platoon(-), B Company, 2nd Battalion, Royal Green Jackets (2 RGJ), with a strength of 20 personnel. Attached in support is 1 Troop, C Squadron, Royal Yeomanry, consisting of 12 personnel."\
     "Both elements are currently staged at GRID: 022059"\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• High mobility provided by the attached light cavalry troop, operating 4x WMIKs equipped with roof-mounted .50 cal heavy machine guns and front-mounted GPMGs."\
     "• Light infantry supported by mobile direct fire assets, allowing rapid manoeuvre between objectives."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
     "• None."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E7978DA92D6A3CA4}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "We are the Irish Republican Army (IRA), Platan team. Our force consists of approximately 45 personnel distributed between our established positions along the MSR and throughout the surrounding terrain. Our team is staging at the most western barn yard."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• We have two occupied machine gun positions: 1x M2 .50 cal and 1x PKM. Refer to maps for their locations."\
     "• Our sapper is equipped with explosive charges, with additional charges available in a small supply box at our staging area. He should use these to establish traps and exploit opportunities against the enemy where possible."\
     "• Our forces are lightly equipped but highly mobile, allowing us to conduct coordinated hit-and-run engagements before breaking contact and repositioning."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>"\
     "At our staging area we have a motorbike, an unarmed UAZ, and one PKM armed UAZ which contains:"\
     "- 1x AT mine"\
     "- 1x Portable ladder"\
     "- 1x Handheld periscope"\
     "- 6x Red flares"\
     "- 4x PKM belts for the UAZ."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRA"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{07F65CCEF60A42E1}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
     "We are to conduct a <b>DELIBERATE ATTACK</b> in order to <b>SWEEP</b> Objectives Dog and Cat before <b>SECURING</b> Objective Bird by clearing and holding."\
     ""\
     "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
     "IRA personnel have been using the farmyards along this route to conduct irregular ambushes against British Army and Garda patrols travelling between Lovetin and Kamoryn. Their attacks have also placed civilian traffic at risk, with several non-combatants caught in the crossfire."\
     ""\
     "Following weeks of intelligence gathering and terrain analysis, these three farmyards have been identified as the most likely staging and ambush locations. Their concealed positions, restricted approaches, and commanding views over the MSR make them ideal for hit-and-run attacks."\
     ""\
     "Our mission is to sweep Objectives Dog and Cat for enemy personnel and materiel before securing Objective Bird, denying the IRA further use of these positions and restoring freedom of movement along the route."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{1BA3DE56915C6A61}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
     "We are to conduct a <b>DELIBERATE DEFENCE</b> by <b>DELAYING & DISRUPTING</b> the advancing British forces in order to deny them control of the MSR."\
     ""\
     "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
     "Our recent ambushes have caused significant disruption along the route. In response, British forces are attempting to push us out of the area and seize our established ambush positions along the MSR."\
     ""\
     "The first two ambush locations are considered expendable and do not need to be defended at all costs. Their loss is acceptable if it allows us to preserve our strength for the final position."\
     ""\
     "The final ambush location must be held. Its loss would severely limit our ability to operate along the route and conduct further attacks. Delay the British advance, disrupt their movements, and prevent them from gaining control of the MSR."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRA"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{AB45FC808192D982}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Comsig"
     m_sContent "<h2>CALLSIGNS</h2>"\
     "• PHQ - 22"\
     "• PLT OC - 22A"\
